@prefix : <http://example.org/orexis/world/hanoi#> .
@prefix hanoi: <http://example.org/orexis/hanoi#> .
@prefix orexis: <http://example.org/orexis#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .

#  A ratified world that is a PUZZLE: the smallest world whose whole point is the search.
#  No sensors, no market, no bus — one agent, three disks, and a goal ratified as a desire.
#  What this world exists to prove is #257's claim: the domain is a plug-in, and this one
#  shipped as an ontology and six ground actions with no Python at all.
#
#  The pegs are the DOMAIN's (T-Box individuals — the actions must name them and code may
#  not name a world instance); the disks are this world's, and how many there are is this
#  file's whole authorship of the puzzle. The on-state is nobody's to author: it is runtime,
#  seeded by whatever poses the puzzle, exactly as readings are.

:world a orexis:World ; orexis:currentVersion :version_1 ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution [ prov:agent <http://example.org/orexis/user/dimonina> ; prov:hadRole orexis:Sovereign ] .
:version_1 a orexis:WorldVersion ; orexis:versionNumber 1 .

:hanoi a orexis:Agent ;
    orexis:localId "hanoi" ;
    rdfs:comment "The mover. It acts for nothing, senses nothing and owes nobody — a pure mind with six levers, which is what makes this world a test of the search and of nothing else." .

:disk_1 a hanoi:Disk ; hanoi:size 1 ; rdfs:label "the small disk" .
:disk_2 a hanoi:Disk ; hanoi:size 2 ; rdfs:label "the middle disk" .
:disk_3 a hanoi:Disk ; hanoi:size 3 ; rdfs:label "the large disk" .
